<details><summary>Click to reveal the fiber geometry</summary>

For a selected active index $p$, the inequalities $m_p+h_p\le m_i+h_i$ define a polyhedron. An escaping basis direction is a recession direction of the corresponding fiber cell. The theorem guarantees one such direction; ties and repeated witnesses can expose several.

</details>

