For background, see [tropical geometry](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropical_geometry), the [pigeonhole principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigeonhole_principle), and [cryptographic hash functions](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptographic_hash_function). The comparison is structural: optimization summaries are designed to reveal winners, whereas cryptographic digests are designed to hide navigable input geometry.
